#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147173 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b754e55b-59fa-50de-b2f9-0444c3177041" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Stand-Alone Exponents"}] :question/id #uuid "6d89587f-dacf-5ce3-95f0-9dd51d307af8" :question/math-academy-id "e-14188" :question/problem "Evaluate $4^2 +(5-3)$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. We start with the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n4^2\\,+\\underbrace{(5-3)}_{\\large\\color{blue} 2} =4^2\\,+ {\\color{blue} 2}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n\\overbrace{4^2}^{\\large\\color{red} 16}+2 = {\\color{red} 16}+2\n$$\n\nFinally, we perform the **A**ddition:\n\n$$\n16+2 = 18\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n4^2 +(5-3)=18\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147174 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0704b3c4-42a9-50f8-a73c-b938a22b3cad" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Outside Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "b035d6d2-aaca-5ea3-8d34-1748b6acfcd6" :question/math-academy-id "e-14191" :question/problem "Calculate $28\\div(7-5)^2$." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. We start with the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n28\\div \\underbrace{(7-5)}_{\\large\\color{blue} 2}{}^2 =28\\div {\\color{blue} 2}^2\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n28\\div\\overbrace{2^2}^{\\large\\color{red} 4} =28\\div {\\color{red} 4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we perform the **D**ivision:\n$28\\div 4 =7$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n28\\div(7-5)^2=7\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147175 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147396 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d7cee42-a91c-5053-8e50-3078d31cc772" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Inside Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "ef92369b-53e8-56ec-b1f2-ee36dbf13839" :question/math-academy-id "e-14193" :question/problem "Evaluate $5\\times \\left(3+2^2\\right)$." :question/worked-solution "According to PEMDAS, we should first calculate the expression inside the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n\\left(3+2^2\\right)\n$$\n\nTo evaluate\n\n$$\n\\left(3+2^2\\right)\n$$\n\nwe should again apply PEMDAS. We start with the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n3\\,+\\overbrace{2^2}^{\\large\\color{blue} 4} =3+ {\\color{blue} 4}\n$$\n\nThen, we perform the **A**ddition:\n\n$$\n3 + 4 = {\\color{red} 7}\n$$\n\nSo we have:\n\n$$\n5\\times \\underbrace{\\left(3+2^2\\right)}_{\\large\\color{red} 7} =5\\times {\\color{red} 7}\n$$\n\nNow that we have calculated the expression inside the **P**arentheses, we can finally move on to the **M**ultiplication:\n\n$$\n5 \\times 7 = 35\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5\\times\\left(3+2^2\\right)=35\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b754e55b-59fa-50de-b2f9-0444c3177041" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Stand-Alone Exponents"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb104bdb-327e-5d61-a7d7-93ae768c8225" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145347} {:answer/id #uuid "001cff45-d0cc-581b-9ddd-002285ecbaa7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145348} {:answer/id #uuid "10cac01a-5129-5332-a842-e3f36aad8365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145349} {:answer/id #uuid "2df9dc9c-0400-5f51-9d7f-e93c8a20c3ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145350} {:answer/id #uuid "685f68b3-5bd8-511d-9b18-08d5251c48df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145351}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4584